t / EBITDA | Net cash ~$53M [Estimate] |\n| Interest coverage | Very high (no material debt) |\n\nVerdict: GOOD to EXCELLENT.\n\n2-5. Capital Allocation Scorecard\n| Item | Score (0-3) |\n|---|---|\n| Buyback efficiency | 0 (share count +4.8% 3-yr CAGR; no buyback) |\n| M&A track record | 1 (acquisition history not fully audited) |\n| Capex efficiency | 2 (plasma centers should add $8-10M+ each at ramp) |\n| Rationality of mix | 2 (selective organic + dividend) |\n| Guidance accuracy | 3 (H1 2026 aligned with guidance) |\n| Insider bonus | +1 (7.2% insider ownership) |\n| **Total** | **9/15 + bonus = 10/18 equivalent** |\n\nSECTION 2.5. INTANGIBLES-ADJUSTED FINANCIALS\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n2.5-1. R&D Capitalization\nR&D expense is not split in the pack [Unconfirmed]. It is likely $5-$8M/year [Assumption]. Capitalizing R&D would lift Adjusted ROIC modestly, but we do not include it in the base valuation.\n\n2.5-2. SBC Treatment\nFY2025 SBC was $1M [Actual]. This is already deducted from GAAP net income; we treat it as a cash expense in FCF. Impact is immaterial.\n\n2.5-3. Operating Leases\nFY2025 operating leases $12M [Actual]. We add this to net debt in the EV bridge.\n\n2.5-4. Brand/Data Assets\nPlasma product franchise value is captured indirectly through higher EBITDA margins. No separate data-asset value is added. [Assumption]\n\n2.5-5. Adjusted ROIC\nGAAP ROIC estimate: NOPAT $20M / invested capital ~$220M = ~9% [Estimate].\nAdjusted EBITDA-based ROIC: ~$42M / ~$220M = ~19% [Estimate].\nThe 10pp gap is due to intangible amortization. We treat amortization as a real cost in valuation.\n\n2.5-6. Owner Earnings (Buffett Style)\nFY2025: NI $20M + D&A $2M - maintenance capex $4M - \u0394WC $11M = $7M [Estimate].\nIf working capital normalizes to 2% of revenue, Owner Earnings ~$15M [Assumption].\n\nSECTION 3. VALUATION \u2014 ENGINE 1: TRADITIONAL DCF + MULTIPLES\n-----------------------------------------------