nario Probabilities, Prices and CIs\n| Scenario | Probability | Assumptions | IV/share |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Bear | 30% | Revenue growth ~5%, EBITDA margin 20%, WACC 11%, KEDRAB share loss, plasma agreement delayed, gross margin <40% | $6.00 |\n| Base | 50% | Forecast as per Section 3 | $11.10 |\n| Bull | 20% | Revenue growth 15% through 2027, margin 28%, WACC 9.5%, M&A accretive, biosimilar distribution upside | $14.00 |\n\nExpected Intrinsic Value = 0.30*$6.00 + 0.50*$11.10 + 0.20*$14.00 = **$10.15**.\n50% CI: $9.50 - $13.00.\n80% CI: $7.50 - $14.50.\n\n4-3. Bayesian Update\nPrior success probability (base rate): 70%.\nEvidence: H1 2026 revenue and adjusted EBITDA each at ~50% of guidance; OCF $17.8M; $50M plasma agreement; dividend maintained.\nLikelihood ratio: ~1.3 [Estimate].\nPosterior = 0.70*1.3 / (0.70*1.3 + 0.30) = **75% success probability**.\n\n4-4/5. Margin of Safety\nMoS = (Expected IV $10.15 - Price $8.24) / Expected IV $10.15 = **18.8%**.\nOn Base IV $11.10, MoS = **25.8%**.\nVerdict: ADEQUATE MoS (15%-30%). Entry should be staged.\n\nSECTION 4.5. TIME HORIZON ARBITRAGE\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCurrent EV/2026E EBITDA of ~8.2x implies the market is pricing an extended low-growth profile (~3-4% terminal growth) [Estimate].\nMy forecast horizon is 3-5 years with 12% then 11% growth. Market horizon appears shorter than 3 years.\nSpread > 2 years => there is a moderate horizon-arbitrage opportunity, but it is not as wide as for a high-multiple growth stock.\n\nSECTION 5. CONVICTION & POSITION SIZING\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n5-1. Conviction Score (max 15)\n| Component | Score (0-3) |\n|---|---|\n| Business quality | 2 |\n| Valuation attractiveness | 3 |\n| Macro alignment | 1 |\n| Thesis clarity / measurable KPIs | 3 |\n| Execution traceability | 3 |\n| **Total** | **12/15 -> HIGH** |\n\n5-2. Conviction Decay\nNo confirming evidence after 6 months