 | (2.4) | Slightly rising [Assumption] |\n| **FCFF (\u2248 FCFE, net cash)** | **24.6** | **32.9** | **38.2** | **41.9** | **46.0** | \u2014 |\n\n### Discount Rate Derivation\n\n| Input | Value | Tag |\n|---|---|---|\n| Risk-Free Rate (10Y Treasury) | **4.70%** | [Actual \u2014 Fed H.15] |\n| Equity Risk Premium | **5.0%** | [Assumption \u2014 Damodaran-style forward ERP] |\n| Beta (used for DCF) | **0.8** | [Assumption \u2014 vendor 0.127 is unverifiable and likely distorted by low-liquidity Israeli ADR structure; a specialty pharma micro-cap has higher system risk than 0.127] |\n| Cost of Equity | **= 4.7% + 0.8 \u00d7 5.0% = 8.7%** | [Arithmetic] |\n| Cost of Debt (pre-tax) | 4.5% | [Assumption] |\n| Tax Rate | 14% | [Assumption] |\n| WACC | **= 8.9% \u2248 9.0%** (\u2248100% equity given net cash) | [Assumption] |\n\n### DCF Value\n\n| Component | Value ($M) | Discount Factor @ 9.0% | PV ($M) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| FY2026E FCFF | 24.6 | 0.917 | 22.6 |\n| FY2027E FCFF | 32.9 | 0.842 | 27.7 |\n| FY2028E FCFF | 38.2 | 0.772 | 29.5 |\n| FY2029E FCFF | 41.9 | 0.708 | 29.7 |\n| FY2030E FCFF | 46.0 | 0.650 | 29.9 |\n| Terminal Value (g = 2.5%) | **726.0** | 0.650 | **471.9** |\n| **Enterprise Value** | | | **611.3** |\n| **+ Net Cash (mid-2026E)** | | | **+50.0** [Estimate] |\n| **Equity Value** | | | **661.3** |\n| **Shares (2026E wtd avg)** | | | **58.5M** [Estimate] |\n| **Intrinsic Value / Share** | | | **$11.30** |\n\n### Multiples Cross-Check\n\n| Metric | Current (T0) | Implied at IV | Peer Rationale |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| P/E (2026E EPS $0.56) | 14.7x | **20.2x** | 20x forward is plausible for a mid-teens grower with net cash; but is near the top of specialty pharma range |\n| EV/EBITDA (2026E) | 8.2x | **11.7x** | Reasonable for a high-single-digit/low-double-digit grower |\n| P/B | 1.73x | 2.3x | Justifiable only if ROE improves above 10% |\n\n**Reconciliation:** The DCF is the primary model. Multiple cross-check supports $10.5\u2013$12.5, consistent with 