--|\n| **Bear** | **25%** | Growth fades to 4% after 2027; EBITDA margin compresses to 20% (competition + mix); WC turns negative; capex overruns; dividend cut; CFO departure signals instability | 2027 Rev $206M, 2030 Rev $226M; exit EBITDA margin 18\u201320%; WACC 9.5% | **$6.70** |\n| **Base** | **50%** | Guidance met; 10.6% growth in 2027, 8% deceleration thereafter; stable 25.5% EBITDA margin; plasma centers deliver contracted revenue; biosimilars add modestly | See Section 3 forecasts | **$11.30** |\n| **Bull** | **25%** | KEDRAB + VARIZIG continue double-digit share gains; biosimilars add $15\u201320M; plasma centers over-deliver; accretive M&A at 60% ROIC; WACC falls to 8.0% | Rev 2030 $330M; exit margin 28%; TV g=3.0% | **$17.00** |\n\n### Bayesian Update Logic\n- **Prior (base rates):** Success probability of a small-cap pharma generating 10%+ growth for 5 years = 30%.\n- **Likelihood from new evidence (2026 H1):** record revenue, reaffirmed guidance, plasma contract signed, biosimilar launches proceeding. Management stated \"another strong year of double-digit growth next year.\"\n- **Posterior:** P(Base) = 50%, P(Bull) = 25%, P(Bear) = 25% \u2014 reflecting partial incorporation of positive evidence but maintaining base-rate skepticism.\n\n### Expected Value & Margin of Safety\n\n| Statistic | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Expected Value per Share | **0.25\u00d7$6.70 + 0.50\u00d7$11.30 + 0.25\u00d7$17.00 = $11.58** |\n| 50% Confidence Interval (Main range) | **$8.50 \u2013 $13.50** [Estimate] |\n| 80% Confidence Interval | **$6.00 \u2013 $16.50** [Estimate] |\n| Margin of Safety (vs $8.24) | **(11.58 \u2212 8.24) / 11.58 = 28.8% \u2192 Adequate** |\n| Margin of Safety (vs Base $11.30) | **27.1% \u2192 Adequate** |\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 4.5 \u2014 TIME HORIZON ARBITRAGE\n\n### Market Implied Horizon\n- At $8.24, with 2026E EPS $0.56, the market pays **~14.7x forward earnings**.\n- At 2026E EBITDA of $51.5M, EV/EBITDA 8.2x. A 10-year horizon DCF (not 5-year) implies the market is capitalizing a mid-single-digit long-run growth rate.\n- **Interpretation:** The market is applying a **defensive-staple multiple** (given its low beta history and 3% dividend) rather than a growth-pharma multiple.\n\n### My Horizon vs Market Horizon\n- My forecast horizon: **5 years explicit + terminal** (DCF horizon ~10+ years).\n- Market-implied horizon: essentially a **perpetuity with 3\u20135% growth**.\n- Spread: **2\u20133 years of incremental visible growth** \u2014 this provides a moderate **time arbitrage opportunity** if management's guidance is credible.\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 5 \u2014 CONVICTION & POSITIONING\n\n### Step 5-1 Conviction Score (Total 15)\n\n| Criterion | Score / 3 | Justification |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1. Business Quality | **2.5** / 3 | Wide moat, net cash, FDA products; but ROE < 8% |\n| 2. Valuation Attractiveness | **2.5** / 3 | 29% MoS, but requires optimistic growth post-2027 |\n| 3. Macro Alignment | **2.0** / 3 | Neutral; high real rates are a mild headwind |\n| 4. Thesis Clarity | **2.5** / 3 | Clear KPIs: KEDRAB/VARIZIG, plasma centers, EBITDA margin |\n| 5. Execution Traceability | **2.0** / 3 | Good guidance track record; but CFO departure creates short-term uncertainty |\n| **Total** | **11.5 / 15** | **High conviction** |\n\n### Step 5-2 Conviction Decay\n- **\u22121 point every 6 months** absent confirming evidence. Monitoring KPIs (Section 8) provide refresh triggers.\n\n### Step 5-3 Sizing Guidelines\n- High conviction (11.5/15) \u2192 Suggested max weight **6\u20138%** before macro/crowding adjustments.\n- Macro Neutral \u2192 no reduction.\n- Crowding low \u2192 no reduction.\n- **Final Normal Portfolio Weight: 5\u20136%** (round down for micro-cap liquidity).\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 5.5 \u2014 BEHAVIORAL & POSITIONING\n\n| Metric | Value | Interpretation | Source/Tag |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Short % Float | **0.42%** | Negligible short interest \u2014 no squeeze potential, no bearish signal | [Aggregator] |\n| Da