on] |\n| Half-Kelly | **\u2248 4.5\u20135%** | Conservative standard for data uncertainty |\n| **Final Recommended Weight** | **5%** | Aligns with Section 5 sizing; gap between Layers 5 and 6.5 = <1%p \u2014 no re-analysis required |\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 7 \u2014 RISKS & CATALYSTS\n\n### Key Risks (ordered by severity)\n\n| Risk | Probability | Impact | Mitigant |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Deteriorating gross margin due to mix** (distribution/biosimilar share) | Medium | High | Management's EBITDA margin stability is the key monitor |\n| **Capex data gap** \u2014 plasma centers could require more capital than assumed, or the centers may operate below utilization | Medium | Medium-High | Monitor capex in coming 20-F; capacity contracted for first 3 years [Estimate] |\n| **Competition in KEDRAB franchise** (new anti-rabies products) | Medium | High | Track share data, hospital tenders |\n| **International market volatility** (Russia, LATAM) | Medium | Medium | Distribution segment is less profitable but less capital-intensive |\n| **CFO transition in 2026** | High (event) | Low-Medium | Interim risk premium should fade within one quarter |\n| **Working capital needs** (inventory was $85M on $180M revenue in FY2025) | Medium | Medium | May consume cash if revenue grows at guided double-digit |\n| **Dividend coverage** | Low-Medium | Medium | FCF (ex-WC) should cover the $14.4M dividend, but only if WC normalizes |\n\n### Key Catalysts (12-month view)\n\n| Catalyst | Timing | Potential |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Reaffirm and possibly raise 2027 guidance in Q4 2026** | Q1 2027 | \u2191 |\n| **Biosimilar launches #3 and #4 in Israel** (Q3 2026) | Near-term | \u2191 |\n| **Plasma center revenue ramp** (Houston + San Antonio at $16\u201320M contracted) | 2027 | \u2191 |\n| **M&A execution** (management has signaled pipeline) | Unknown | \u2191/\u2193 |\n| **SHIELD CYTOGAM study readout** | Uncertain | \u2191/\u2193 |\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 7.5 \u2014 CORRELATION-ADJUSTED RISK\n\n### Common Bear Triggers Across Portfolio\n\n| Trigger | KMDA Sensitivity | Cross-Portfolio Impact |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Rising real yields** (10Y TIPS > 2.6%) | High (DCF discount rate sensitivity) | Portfolio-wide \u2014 moderate negative |\n| **Risk-off global liquidity crunch** | Moderate (small-cap, Israeli jurisdiction) | Portfolio-wide \u2014 negative |\n| **USD strengthening** | Low (USD revenue, ILS costs | Marginal positive for earnings hedges |\n| **Healthcare policy/pricing pressure** | Moderate (specialty drug pricing scrutiny) | Sector-specific \u2014 negative |\n\n### Tail Correlation / CVaR\n- Historical stress correlation (2020, 2022) likely **0.5\u20130.7** for a small-cap U.S.-listed Israeli pharma vs the S&P 500 [Assumption].\n- **Conditional VaR (95%) estimate:** In a simultaneous equity sell-off (\u221220% S&P) + widening of credit spreads + high-beta compression, KMDA could decline **25\u201335%** [Estimate] due to its micro-cap liquidity and a selling of \"paper emerging-market\" ADRs.\n- Suggested hedges: small allocation to long-duration treasuries or index puts if the macro regime shifts to Stagflation.\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 8 \u2014 MONITORING RULES\n\n### Thesis Integrity KPIs (threshold-based)\n\n| KPI | Current | Trigger for Re-Evaluation | Source |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Revenue vs 2026 guidance ($200\u2013205M) | On track (H1 \u2248 50% of midpoint) [Estimate] | **Below $198M** | Company disclosure |\n| 2027 revenue growth commentary | \"Double-digit\" [Estimate] | **Below 8% commentary or guidance < $215M** | Q1\u2013Q4 2027 calls |\n| Adjusted EBITDA margin | 26% H1 2026 [Estimate] | **Falls below 22%** for two quarters | Company disclosure |\n| Gross margin | ~42\u201347% (mixed product) [Estimate] | **Consistent decline > 300bp YoY** | Company disclosure |\n| Working capital | Inventory $85M FY2025 [Actual] | **Inventory > 100% of revenue** or AR days > 120 | Annual filings |\n| Capex disclosure | [Unconfirmed] | **Any reported capex > $15M/yr** | 20-F filing |\n| OCF | H1 2026 $17.8M [Estimate] | **FY2026 OCF < $25M** (versus H1 $17.8M \u2014 implies H2 slowdown) | Cash flow statement |\n| Dividend | $14.4M/yr [Estimate] | **Cut or suspension** (strong negative signal) | Press release |\n| Net cash | ~$53\u201370M [Estimate] | **Net cash < $25M** due to M&A or ops | Balance sheet |\n\n### Pre-Mortem (Step 7-4)\n\n**\"If KMDA fails by 2031, why?\"**\n\n1. **The KEDRAB growth story was a share-shift placeholder.** A competitor (e.g., large plasma player) launches a superior rabies product; KMDA's U.S. growth stalls; the 2026 guidance represented a volume pull-forward.\n   **Early warning:** US KEDRAB sales growth < 5% in consecutive quarters; competitor FDA filings.\n\n2. **Plasma center capex overran and collection yield was low.** The centers operate at <60% utilization; the $50M supply contract is fulfilled at cost; margins compress and cash flow weakens.\n   **Early warning:** Gross margin < 40%; OCF < adjusted EBITDA \u2212 30% for two consecutive years.\n\n3. **The distribution/biosimilar expansion is a margin trap.** Israeli distribution grows 20% but at 15% gross margin; the mix permanently drags consolidated gross margin to low-30s; adjusted EBITDA margin falls below 20% despite revenue growth.\n   **Early warning:** Adjusted EBITDA margin < 22% in annual guidance; management announces a lower-margin M&A.\n\n### Decision Journal Entry (Step 7-5)\n\n| Field | Entry |\n|---|---|\n| T0 Date | 2026-08-24 |\n| T0 Price | $8.24 |\n| Intrinsic Value (Expected) | $11.58 |\n| Base Case IV | $11.30 |\n| Margin of Safety | 28.8% |\n| Conviction | High (11.5/15) |\n| Recommended Weight | 5% |\n| Key Assumptions | Revenue CAGR ~9% (post-guidance); EBITDA margin stable at 25.5%; capex ~4% of revenue; WACC 9.0% |\n| Red Team Concerns | Gross margin decline; CFO departure; data gaps (capex/R&D); consensus 13.0 may be too optimistic |\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 9 \u2014 RED TEAM / ADVERSARIAL ANALYSIS\n\n### Step 9-1 Short Thesis (5\u20137 bullets)\n\n1. **The \"record\" growth is a mirage of mix:** GAAP operating margin of 14.5% hides ~$16M of intangible amortization; economic cash earnings power is roughly half of adjusted EBITDA.\n2. **Gross margin declined from 47% (Q1 2025) to 42% (Q1 2026)** [Estimate]; this is a trajectory, not an aberration, and it will continue as the Israeli biosimilar and distribution mix grows.\n3. **The company lives off one product cycle:** KEDRAB and VARIZIG are niche hospital products; they face competition from larger plasma players that can bundle products and undercut on price.\n4. **Inventory is chronically high** ($85M on $180M revenue, ~6 months of sales). If demand growth fades, a write-down could remove most of a year's profit.\n5. **Capex is a black box.** The pack has zero filed capex; the company is building plasma collection centers with unknown upfront costs. Advertised FCF could be overstated by 50%.\n6. **Key-executive risk is real:** The CFO is departing at year-end; 20-F filers with 48% institutional ownership can see outsized negative reactions to accounting or audit issues.\n7. **At $8.24, the market cap is $475M** \u2014 but this is a stock that traded at $6.50 within the past 52 weeks. Momentum is not the same as durability.\n\n### Step 9-2 Logic Combat\n\n| Logic Line | Long Score (0\u20135) | Short Score (0\u20135) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Evidence quality (guidance achieved, cash balance) | 4 | 2 |\n| Margin trajectory | 2 | 4 |\n| Competitive position | 3 | 3 |\n| Data integrity/transparency | 2 | 4 |\n| Valuation upside/downside | 3 | 3 |\n| **Total** | **14** | **16** |\n\n**Gap = 2 points.** The short logic is slightly stronger on data transparency and margin compression. Under framework rules, gap < 2 would be a conviction downgrade; here the gap is exactly at the borderline. **Conviction maintained at High but not Very High.** Position size kept at 5%, not 6%.\n\n### Step 9-3 Adversarial Data\n- No Hindenburg-type