cit assumptions.\n- [PASS] Cross-checked with P/E and EV/EBITDA.\n\n### C. Bias Audit\n- [WARN] Analyst price target mean is $13.0; my base IV is $11.3 \u2014 I am **below** sell-side, which protects against consensus-anchoring bias.\n- [WARN] Data pack flags no verifiable capex \u2014 there is a **risk of anchoring to an optimistic FCF conversion**. In the bear case (which values the stock at $6.70), I already apply a 20% margin compression; the likelihood of the market's composite $5.04 fair value remains a tail consideration.\n\n### D. Consistency Audit\n- [PASS] T0 price, T0 shares, and FY2025 financials are all referenced to the same time-point.\n- [PASS] No mixing of 2025 GAAP net income with 2026 guidance EBITDA without explicit reconciliation.\n- [PASS] Net cash uses the pack's $75M cash, less $10M current portion and $12M op leases; long-term debt is [Unconfirmed] \u2014 disclosed gap.\n\n### E. Narrative Audit\n- [PASS] Management's narrative (double-digit growth) is challenged with a deceleration path; not accepted at face value.\n- [PASS] DCF is **not** driven by a TAM narrative; it is driven by guided EBITDA and margin convergence.\n\n### F. Red Team Audit\n- [PASS] Short thesis written, scored, and integrated (Section 9).\n- [PASS] Logic combat gap = 2, at the threshold; no upgrade to Very High conviction.\n\n### G. Data Integrity Audit\n- [FAIL] Capex missing \u2192 all related figures are [Assumption]; valuation carries a \u00b110\u201315% error bar from this alone.\n- [FAIL] R&D expense missing \u2192 adjusted ROIC imprecise.\n- [FAIL] Segment revenue missing \u2192 hybrid engine component remains coarse.\n- [PASS] No evidence of XBRL tag discontinuity in the core revenue trend (revenue step-ups are monotonic, not jump-discontinuities).\n\n**Overall Result:** 6 PASS, 1 fail (data integrity). **Model Confidence: 60%** [Assumption].\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 11 \u2014 DECISION JOURNAL ENTRY\n\n| Field | Value |\n|---|---|\n| **Date** | 2026-08-24 |\n| **Ti