io** | **\u2248 2.2 : 1** |\n| **Portfolio Role** | Defensive specialty-pharma core; low-beta; dividend yield ~3%; diversifier against tech/growth concentration |\n\n### Final Comments\nKamada is a **reasonably-priced compounder** with a solid balance sheet, FDA-regulated product portfolio, and visible contracted growth from its plasma center strategy. The value proposition is clear: the market prices it as a **defensive 3% dividend stock with ~8x EV/EBITDA**, while the company is delivering **low-double-digit organic growth** with 26% adjusted EBITDA margins.\n\nThe analysis is **tempered** by four unresolved questions: (1) the true capex intensity of the plasma-center roll-out, (2) the trajectory of consolidated gross margin as mix shifts, (3) the lack of segment-level transparency, and (4) a CFO transition. These uncertainties are why the position size is 5%, not 7\u20138%, and why the entry is split into two tranches.\n\n**Discipline statement:** If any of the primary KPIs in Section 8 are violated, the thesis is void and the position should be re-evaluated \u2014 ideally before a 20% drawdown. If the stock reaches $13.50 without KPI confirmation, reduce to 3% weight and let remaining exposure run on updated evidence.\n\n### AUDIT COMPLIANCE SUMMARY\n- [PASS] DCF not used as sole conclusion \u2014 cross-checked with multiples\n- [PASS] No peer-multiple-only conclusion\n- [PASS] No TAM narrative-only conclusion\n- [PASS] Macro is integrated\n- [PASS] Position sizing and monitoring KPIs attached\n- [PASS] Core monetization (EBITDA guidance) not mixed with future optionality (biosimilar/M&A)\n- [PASS] Platform premium not used without numerical backing\n- [PASS] No vague phrases used\n- [PASS] Data gaps labelled [Unconfirmed] or [Assumption]\n- [PASS] Base rates included\n- [PASS] Red team analysis included\n- [PASS] Pre-mortem included\n- [PASS] Layer 5 vs Layer 6.5 sizing gap = <1%p \u2014 no re-analysis required\n- [PASS] Output in English, single block, all 13 