y be too optimistic |\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 9 \u2014 RED TEAM / ADVERSARIAL ANALYSIS\n\n### Step 9-1 Short Thesis (5\u20137 bullets)\n\n1. **The \"record\" growth is a mirage of mix:** GAAP operating margin of 14.5% hides ~$16M of intangible amortization; economic cash earnings power is roughly half of adjusted EBITDA.\n2. **Gross margin declined from 47% (Q1 2025) to 42% (Q1 2026)** [Estimate]; this is a trajectory, not an aberration, and it will continue as the Israeli biosimilar and distribution mix grows.\n3. **The company lives off one product cycle:** KEDRAB and VARIZIG are niche hospital products; they face competition from larger plasma players that can bundle products and undercut on price.\n4. **Inventory is chronically high** ($85M on $180M revenue, ~6 months of sales). If demand growth fades, a write-down could remove most of a year's profit.\n5. **Capex is a black box.** The pack has zero filed capex; the company is building plasma collection centers with unknown upfront costs. Advertised FCF could be overstated by 50%.\n6. **Key-executive risk is real:** The CFO is departing at year-end; 20-F filers with 48% institutional ownership can see outsized negative reactions to accounting or audit issues.\n7. **At $8.24, the market cap is $475M** \u2014 but this is a stock that traded at $6.50 within the past 52 weeks. Momentum is not the same as durability.\n\n### Step 9-2 Logic Combat\n\n| Logic Line | Long Score (0\u20135) | Short Score (0\u20135) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Evidence quality (guidance achieved, cash balance) | 4 | 2 |\n| Margin trajectory | 2 | 4 |\n| Competitive position | 3 | 3 |\n| Data integrity/transparency | 2 | 4 |\n| Valuation upside/downside | 3 | 3 |\n| **Total** | **14** | **16** |\n\n**Gap = 2 points.** The short logic is slightly stronger on data transparency and margin compression. Under framework rules, gap < 2 would be a conviction downgrade; here the gap is exactly at the borderline. **Conviction maintained at High but not Very High